RecorderNode::createBusFromRecording copied the first recorded channel into every
channel, so a capture of a stereo graph reported its left channel twice: a source
panned right recorded as silence. Each channel now takes its own recording and a
mono recording fills every channel, as speakers up-mix it. A channel that appears
or disappears mid-recording stays frame-aligned with the first (lazy growth
appended a full set of channels again and left later ones short), and mixing to
mono averages the channels recorded rather than reading past them.

diff --git a/src/extended/RecorderNode.cpp b/src/extended/RecorderNode.cpp
index 89ba188..0c8e244 100644
--- a/src/extended/RecorderNode.cpp
+++ b/src/extended/RecorderNode.cpp
